          "id": "d5234a23fce66217e45329798b2e66dad4f7f30f",
          "message": "research: GPT-5.6/codex stand-in ZK soundness audit for sq-qhy4 [FABLE-5] (#1947)\n\nAI-conducted (GPT-5.6/codex) stand-in for the external accredited-cryptographer\naudit (sq-qhy4/CR-G1), cross-checked against code. Verdict AI-AUDITED:\nissues-found — 0 critical, 1 HIGH (NEW), 1 medium (already CR-G8), 2 low.\n\nHIGH H-1 (sq-l15mi): in-circuit issuer.nr Schnorr + sig::public_key_from_hex\nlack the prime-order subgroup check the clear-path sig::verify has → torsion-key\nforgery on the hidden-issuer path (bounded by KeySet curation).\n\nHonest non-human caveat throughout: reduces risk, does NOT substitute for human\nsign-off; does NOT close sq-qhy4. Several dossier gaps found already-closed on\nmain (join binding wired; committed revocation deployed).\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
